  "editorial_notes": "Solo podcast recording, single condenser microphone, home studio with moderate room reflections. Raw recording was 47 minutes 27 seconds; edited to 42 minutes 43 seconds by removing: 2 false starts (top and tail), 8 extended filler-word sequences ('um', 'uh'), 1 phone notification sound at 23:41, and 3 sections where the host went significantly off-topic. High-pass at 120 Hz eliminates HVAC rumble. Parametric EQ: -2.5 dB at 240 Hz removes the boxy resonance characteristic of the recording room, +1 dB at 1800 Hz adds presence for voice intelligibility, +1.5 dB at 5 kHz adds air and clarity without introducing sibilance. De-esser clamps the 7.2 kHz sibilance range which was occasionally harsh on the 'S' and 'C' sounds. Compressor at 3.5:1 controls dynamic range without sounding over-processed — RMS detection chosen over peak for smoother result on voice. Gate set very low (-52 dB) to only mute true silence, not quiet speech. Final integrated loudness -16.8 LUFS is appropriate for podcast distribution (Apple Podcasts target: -16 LUFS).",
